## API reference

### Field

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `name:` | `String` | - | The control's `name`. |
| `error:` | `String` | - | A server-side message; renders the field invalid. |
| `invalid:` | `Boolean` | - | Render invalid without a message. |
| `disabled:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Disables the control and dims the parts. |
| `validation_mode:` | `:submit`, `:blur`, `:change` | `:submit` | When the constraints are checked. |
| `messages:` | `Hash` | `{}` | Text per failure: `value_missing`, `type_mismatch`, `pattern_mismatch`, `too_short`, `too_long`, `range_underflow`, `range_overflow`, `step_mismatch`, `bad_input`. |
| `id:` | `String` | random | Prefix for the parts' ids. |

Events: `ui--field:valid` and `ui--field:invalid` (with `{ failure }`).

### FieldLabel, FieldDescription

A `<label>` pointing at the control, and the help text linked with `aria-describedby`.

### FieldError

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `match:` | `Symbol` | - | Show this block only for one failure (`:value_missing`…). Without it, shows the field's message. |

### Fieldset, FieldsetLegend

A `<fieldset>` labelled by its legend; `disabled: true` disables every control inside.

## Accessibility

- The label is a real `<label for>`; the description and any showing error are listed in the control's
  `aria-describedby`.
- Invalid controls get `aria-invalid="true"`; the error is a `role="alert"` region, announced when it appears.
- The error slides open with a height transition that is skipped under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
